  "question": {
    "text": "The structures of beryllium chloride in the solid state and vapour phase, respectively, are:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "chain and chain",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "dimeric and chain",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "chain and dimeric",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "dimeric and dimeric",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "BeCl<sub>2</sub> exists as (BeCl<sub>2</sub>)n polymeric chain in solid form, while BeCl<sub>2</sub> exists as dimer in vapour phase because <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> has vacant orbital and it is electron deficient.<br />In vapour state<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0095_8e4a97a1d175.png\" /><br />In solid state<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0095_d678c1ecb4af.png\" />"
  }
